    "2117255670403870949": {
      "account_followers": 7595,
      "account_handle": "FXTaka6000",
      "account_name": "TAKA🦅",
      "bookmarks": 11,
      "content_en": "In Japan it's all lumped together as \"overseas FX\", but FX is fundamentally a global\nfinancial business.\nIn the UK there's INFINOX, in Australia IC Markets, and Exness and ATFX also have entities and bases in multiple countries, operating around the world.\nIn 2023 ATFX acquired Rakuten Securities Australia, and the following year it switched to the ATFX brand.\nEvery country has its own FX brokers, and on top of that, while following each country's rules,\nthey expand their business overseas too.\nJapan has domestic FX companies too, and that's fine.\nBut why does Japan separate domestic and overseas so much?\nI understand investor protection is needed,\nand I don't take that lightly, but regulating and closing off the market are different things.\nRather than just protecting the domestic market,\nI think we could consider an environment where people can properly use the world's financial services under proper\nrules, competing with the world.\nNot toward closing, but toward connecting with the world.\nThat's what I think🦅",
      "content_original": "日本では「海外FX」って\nひとまとめにされるけど そもそもFXはグローバルな\n金融ビジネスなんよね\nイギリスにはINFINOX オーストラリアにはIC Markets ExnessやATFXも複数の国に法人や拠点を持って 世界中で事業を展開してる\n2023年にはATFXが楽天証券オーストラリアを買収して 翌年にはATFXブランドに切り替わった\nどの国にも自国のFXブローカーがある そのうえで 各国のルールに従いながら\n海外にも事業を広げてる\n日本にも国内FX会社がある それはそれでいい\nでも なんで日本は国内と海外をここまで分けて考えるのか\n投資家保護が必要なのは分かるし \nそこを軽く見るつもりもない ただ 規制することと市場を閉ざすことは別の話\n国内市場を守るだけじゃなく \n世界と競争して 世界の金融サービスをちゃんとした\nルールのもとで使える環境を考えてもいいんじゃないかな\n閉じる方向じゃなく世界とつながる方向へ\nオレはそう思ってる🦅",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:01:03Z",
      "enriched_at": "2026-11-03T07:52:29Z",
      "enriched_by": "copilot",
      "exclude_reason": null,
